---
title: User Registration API Sequence Diagram (Java Spring Boot)
---
sequenceDiagram
    participant Client
    participant UserRegistrationController
    participant UserService
    participant UserRepository
    participant UserProfileRepository
    participant PasswordEncoder
    participant EmailService
    participant GlobalExceptionHandler

    Client->>UserRegistrationController: POST /users/register (UserRegistrationRequest)
    UserRegistrationController->>UserService: registerUser(request)
    UserService->>UserRepository: existsByEmail(email)
    alt Email already exists
        UserService-->>UserRegistrationController: throw UserAlreadyExistsException
        UserRegistrationController->>GlobalExceptionHandler: handleUserAlreadyExists()
        GlobalExceptionHandler-->>Client: 409 Conflict (ErrorResponse)
    else Email does not exist
        UserService->>PasswordEncoder: encode(password)
        UserService->>UserRepository: save(User)
        UserService->>UserProfileRepository: save(UserProfile)
        UserService->>EmailService: sendRegistrationConfirmation(email, name)
        UserService-->>UserRegistrationController: UserResponse
        UserRegistrationController-->>Client: 201 Created (UserResponse)
    end
    Note over UserService,UserRegistrationController: Validation errors or other exceptions are handled by GlobalExceptionHandler and returned as ErrorResponse
